<h1>Build an on-call escalation line with VoiceML.</h1>
<p class="lede">The Ghostbusters run a fictional paranormal response line. Urgent calls ring the on-call team one person at a time until someone answers, each kind of emergency has its own call order, and routine reports are recorded for the morning. It runs on two documents published on voiceml.org, with no application server.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Free trial</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ site.voicemlReferenceUrl }}/verbs/dial/">&lt;Dial&gt; reference</a>
</p>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>What callers get</h2>
	<ul class="features-grid">
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "hash" %}</span>
			<h3>Triage first</h3>
			<p>Press 1 for an active haunting, 2 for a containment unit emergency, or 3 to report a sighting. Only the first two wake anyone up.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "list-check" %}</span>
			<h3>An on-call chain</h3>
			<p><code>&lt;Dial sequential="true"&gt;</code> rings Peter, then Ray, then Winston, 15 seconds each, and connects the first one who answers.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "diagram-3" %}</span>
			<h3>A chain per emergency</h3>
			<p>Containment emergencies have their own call order: Egon first, then Ray.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "arrow-right-circle" %}</span>
			<h3>A way out when nobody answers</h3>
			<p>After the chain, the caller can ring the team again or leave a report, and a caller whose call was answered just hangs up.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "record-circle" %}</span>
			<h3>Routine reports, recorded</h3>
			<p>Sightings and inspection requests are taken as a recording of up to two minutes, so nobody is called for them.</p>
		</li>
	</ul>
</section>

