<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Before you start</h2>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>A VoiceML account with a phone number.</strong> See <a href="/voiceml/">VoiceML</a> or <a href="/signup/">start a free trial</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>The phone numbers of the people on call</strong>, in E.164 format, and the order to call them in for each kind of emergency.</li>
	</ol>
	<div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
		<p><strong>The numbers in these documents are fictional.</strong> They use the 555-0100 to 555-0199 range, which is set aside for fiction. Replace every <code>&lt;Number&gt;</code> with a real on-call number before you publish.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 1: Publish the goodbye document</h2>
	<p>Every <code>&lt;Record&gt;</code> needs an <code>action</code>; without one, the runtime requests the current document again and the caller hears the prompt and records a second time. This document is that <code>action</code>.</p>
	<p class="code-block-header">goodbye.xml</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>{{ voicemlSamples["ghostbusters-dispatch"].goodbye | escape }}</code></pre>
	<p>Paste it at <a href="{{ site.voicemlPublisherUrl }}">voiceml.org</a>, validate it, and publish. It contains no Liquid, so it is served from an <code>/s/</code> URL. Keep the URL exactly as returned, <code>key</code> included. The key is a shared secret, so don&rsquo;t post the URL publicly.</p>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 2: Publish the main document</h2>
	<p>Replace <code>GOODBYE_URL</code> with the URL from step 1, and replace the on-call numbers with your own. Then publish it, and set the <code>/r/</code> URL it returns as the phone number&rsquo;s voice URL.</p>
	<p class="code-block-header">main.xml</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>{{ voicemlSamples["ghostbusters-dispatch"].main | escape }}</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 3: Test it</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Call the number and press 1. The first on-call phone rings; don&rsquo;t answer it.</li>
		<li>After 15 seconds the second phone rings. Answer it, and you are connected to the caller.</li>
		<li>Call again, press 1, and let every phone ring out. You hear the offer to try again or leave a report; press 3 and leave one.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>How the escalation works</h2>
	<p>The menu&rsquo;s <code>&lt;Gather&gt;</code> has no <code>action</code>, so the key the caller presses comes back to the same document as <code>Digits</code> and picks a branch. Branches 1 and 2 each hold a <code>&lt;Dial&gt;</code> with several <code>&lt;Number&gt;</code> nouns:</p>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<caption>The &lt;Dial&gt; attributes this example sets</caption>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col">Attribute</th>
					<th scope="col">Value</th>
					<th scope="col">Effect</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>sequential</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Rings the numbers one at a time, in document order, until one answers. Without it, they all ring at once and the first to answer wins.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>timeout</code></td><td><code>15</code></td><td>How long each number rings before the next one is tried.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ringTone</code></td><td><code>us</code></td><td>The caller hears a US ringback tone while the chain rings.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p>The on-call phone shows the caller&rsquo;s own number, because a <code>&lt;Dial&gt;</code> without a <code>callerId</code> passes it through.</p>
	<p>A <code>&lt;Dial&gt;</code> without an <code>action</code> continues to the next verb whether the call was answered or not, and a voiceml.org document can&rsquo;t read the dial result to tell the two apart. So instead of guessing, the line asks: &ldquo;If no one answered, press 1 to try the on-call team again, or press 3 to leave a report. Otherwise, you may hang up.&rdquo; That <code>&lt;Gather&gt;</code> has no <code>action</code> either, so the key the caller presses runs the matching branch of the menu again.</p>
</section>

