<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Limits of this design</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>The caller decides what happens after the chain.</strong> To retry or take a report automatically when nobody answered, point the <code>&lt;Dial&gt;</code>&rsquo;s <code>action</code> at your own server, which receives <code>DialCallStatus</code> and can answer with VoiceML of its own.</li>
		<li><strong>A phone&rsquo;s voicemail can end the chain.</strong> If an on-call phone sends calls to voicemail before <code>timeout</code> runs out, the voicemail answers and the chain stops there. Keep <code>timeout</code> shorter than your team&rsquo;s phones take to go to voicemail.</li>
		<li><strong>The rotation is fixed in the document.</strong> Published documents can&rsquo;t be edited, so changing who is on call means publishing a new document and pointing the number at its URL. To pick the chain by day of the week, combine this with the time checks in the <a href="/support/voiceml/build-business-hours-routing-with-voiceml/">business-hours example</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>Reports stay on your account.</strong> To have each report emailed, add the VoiceML Dashboard&rsquo;s voicemail callback to the <code>&lt;Record&gt;</code>, as the <a href="/support/voiceml/build-a-pbx-with-voiceml/">PBX example</a> does.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

